    {
      "name": "book-preview",
      "type": "registry:block",
      "title": "Book Preview",
      "description": "Accessible shadcn-compatible book preview with a lightweight default page engine. Optional scroll, curl, spread, archival-curl, WebGL, and PDF adapters are separate.",
      "registryDependencies": [
        "button",
        "toggle-group",
        "tooltip",
        "dropdown-menu",
        "sheet",
        "slider",
        "alert",
        "empty",
        "skeleton",
        "separator",
        "spinner",
        "input",
        "popover",
        "tabs"
      ],
      "dependencies": ["@tabler/icons-react"],
      "docs": "The default installation includes the lightweight page engine only. Optional engines (premier, scroll, curl, spread, archival-curl, webgl, pdf) live in the book-preview-engines item and require pdfjs-dist, three, @react-three/fiber, @react-three/drei, and maath when those modes are enabled. Requires Base UI primitives (a base-* shadcn project): usage relies on render props, array-valued Slider and ToggleGroup state. Orientation styling keys off Base UI's data-orientation attribute. Do not treat qualitative capability labels as measured performance guarantees. The core also ships highlights, notes, bookmarks and freehand ink (pen, marker, eraser; page-relative strokes) (CSS Custom Highlight API; controlled via annotations/onAnnotationsChange or persisted with persistAnnotations), the Aa reading settings, shareable URL state (urlState), auto-hiding fullscreen chrome, and a provider-agnostic Ask panel (pass an `ai` adapter from ai.ts: on-device, OpenAI-compatible/Ollama, or your own route). Tabs and Popover rely on Base UI.",
